data.content:
Your labels are blank because you're missing two things:

1. **No `BindingContext`** — the page doesn't know which ViewModel to bind to.
2. **No `x:DataType`** — you should use compiled bindings for type safety and performance.

**Fix:**

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:YourApp.ViewModels"
             x:DataType="vm:YourViewModel">
    <VerticalStackLayout>
        <Label Text="{Binding Title}" />
        <Label Text="{Binding Description}" />
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ContentPage>
```

Then set the `BindingContext` in code-behind or via dependency injection:

```csharp
// Option A: code-behind constructor
public MyPage()
{
    InitializeComponent();
    BindingContext = new YourViewModel();
}

// Option B: DI (preferred) — register in MauiProgram.cs,
// then inject via constructor
public MyPage(YourViewModel vm)
{
    InitializeComponent();
    BindingContext = vm;
}
```

Also ensure your ViewModel implements `INotifyPropertyChanged` (or inherits `ObservableObject` from the CommunityToolkit.Mvvm) so the UI updates when properties change.
